Description:
  Calibrates agent-based epidemic models built with the R package
  'epiworldR' (SEIR and SIR) from daily counts of new infections, cases or
  hospital admissions. Ships DeepIMC, a trained bidirectional LSTM that
  calibrates a window of 15 to 365 days from any part of an epidemic in well
  under a second, with a 95% range for the basic reproduction number R0, and
  the four standard calibration methods it is compared with (ABC-SMC,
  ABC-MCMC, differential evolution and Nelder-Mead), all through one
  function. Whole curves can be smoothed and split where their growth rate
  changes (segmented regression), each part calibrated on its own, and the
  epidemic the estimates imply run again with the agent-based model; a part
  can be run on past a known intervention to give the cases expected without
  it. Includes the real epidemic data of the paper (COVID-19, influenza, SARS,
  Ebola, MERS, smallpox and measles) with dated interventions. Implements the
  methods described in Najafzadehkhoei, Vega Yon, Modenesi and Meyer (2025)
  <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2509.07013>.
